WEBVTT

00:12:58.667 --> 00:13:02.018
markets inevitably create
more problems than they solve.

00:13:02.042 --> 00:13:03.309
Climate change,

00:13:03.333 --> 00:13:05.309
the great financial crisis of 2008

00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:07.042
are two easy examples.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.976
The second rule is

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:15.000
that inclusion creates economic growth.

00:13:16.208 --> 00:13:18.768
So the neoliberal idea

00:13:18.792 --> 00:13:21.393
that inclusion is this fancy luxury

00:13:21.417 --> 00:13:25.917
to be afforded if and when we have growth
is both wrong and backwards.

00:13:27.208 --> 00:13:29.667
The economy is people.